From 97b68640bfa54474a4d62c44817dc8620947904d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mrinohk <5554998+Mrinohk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:35:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07/31] Fuse the GDN gated output norm: rms_norm * w * silu(z)
 in one kernel

The gated delta net's output is rms_norm(x) * ssm_norm * silu(z), which ran as
stock's fused norm*weight plus the fused silu*mul, two launches per layer.
rms_norm_f32 gets a do_gate variant that takes z in the add operand's slot,
loads x, w and z before the row reduction (rows are 128 wide, one value per
thread) and stores silu(z) * (norm * w), the same products in the same order,
so the result is bit-exact.

The z projection was scheduled between the norm and the gate because nothing
needed it earlier; qwen35moe's build_norm_gated now expands it first so the
four nodes are adjacent. That only changes the node order. The matcher uses
ggml_can_fuse_subgraph since the silu takes z, not the previous node. Only on
with GGML_CUDA_P60_MMVQ=1; GGML_CUDA_P60_FUSE_NORM_GATE=0 turns it off.

2x P100: decode wall 15.61 -> 15.49 ms/token in the trace, MTP 8-prompt
110.4 -> 110.85 t/s (+0.4%, two rounds). Wikitext KLD at ub=1 vs the previous
commit: 0, same top 100%; MTP outputs byte-identical to the previous commit.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
